# Trivy ignore list for findings that cannot be remediated by this repo.
#
# Each entry below is a CRITICAL finding where the upstream vendor has
# explicitly marked the issue "will_not_fix" for the Debian release our base
# images are built on - there is no patched package version to upgrade to,
# so `apt-get upgrade` can never resolve it. Re-check periodically in case
# that changes; see the linked advisory for the current vendor status.

# zlib1g on Debian 12 (bookworm) - affects details, productpage, ratings
# (all Debian "slim" base images). Debian Security Tracker marks this
# will_not_fix for bookworm as of this writing.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-45853
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3-0 on Debian 12 (bookworm) - affects productpage. No patched
# package version exists yet for this Debian release (Trivy reports status
# "affected" with no Fixed Version) - nothing to upgrade to.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-7458
CVE-2025-7458

# gosu (a small Go-based privilege-drop tool baked into the official mysql
# and mongo Docker images) is compiled against an older Go stdlib with this
# CVE. Confirmed present even on mysql:latest and the newest available
# mongo:8.x tag as of this writing - Docker's official images haven't been
# rebuilt with a patched Go toolchain yet. We don't control gosu's build
# process from our Dockerfile; re-check when newer tags are published.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68121
CVE-2025-68121
